any of these albums."

00:09:19.198 --> 00:09:20.031
It was like--

00:09:20.031 --> 00:09:22.286
And then she's like,
"What are you looking at?"

00:09:22.286 --> 00:09:24.995
That's not how it works in
2030, that's how it will work.

00:09:24.995 --> 00:09:28.460
I'm like, "I recognize
that Harry styles album,

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.156
the one with watermelon sugar on it."

00:09:30.156 --> 00:09:32.771
Okay, you're really narrowing it down.

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:35.005
Whoever this is, is gonna know who it was.

00:09:35.005 --> 00:09:37.621
Yeah, maybe that's why I
shouldn't be talking about it.

00:09:37.621 --> 00:09:39.281
It's someone who works for us,

00:09:39.281 --> 00:09:42.131
who was a woman who has
albums in the background.

00:09:42.131 --> 00:09:44.378
No, it's not someone who works for us.

00:09:44.378 --> 00:09:46.663
It's someone who works for the company--

00:09:46.663 --> 00:09:47.508
Company who's doing the training

00:09:47.508 --> 00:09:49.144
That's putting on the class.

00:09:49.144 --> 00:09:50.888
I do not know this person--

00:09:50.888 --> 00:09:51.842
That changes things.

00:09:51.842 --> 00:09:53.845
This person does not work for me.

00:09:53.845 --> 00:09:56.096
That's important to me.

00:09:56.096 --> 00:10:00.184
Because then as I'm
looking at these albums,

00:10:00.184 --> 00:10:02.472
